     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled dose of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. The single dose of 1700 mg is also well above the usual maximum of 1000 mg per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nHere are some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **1700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, a more typical regimen.\n\nPlease tell me the dose you want, or confirm that 1700 mg three times daily is what you intend. If it is, I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first. I'll enter the order once you reply."
      }
     ],
